From 1f7cb79884e60b7f9eaa6cd37bd143d5cd712d77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: raawaa-engine <engine@raawaa.local>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 01:37:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ci): load axe as a same-origin external script under the
 strict CSP

PR #158 tightened the production CSP to `script-src 'self'
https://connect.facebook.net`. Every accessibility harness still injected
axe-core with `page.add_script_tag(content=AXE)`, which appends an inline
<script> and is therefore blocked. That is why the accessibility audit, the
Chromium serum suite and the WebKit serum suite failed while the pages
themselves were fine.

- New scripts/axe_loader.py is the single implementation: it registers a
  same-origin, test-only route (/__test__/axe.min.js) that Playwright fulfils
  from scripts/vendor/axe.min.js, injects axe with `add_script_tag(url=...)`,
  and waits for window.axe. Nothing is added to the production build and no
  CSP source is added or relaxed.
- Removed the ineffective `Page.setBypassCSP` CDP call from axe-audit.py.
  Bypassing the policy would have hidden the very regression the PR exists to
  prevent.
- axe-audit.py, a11y-audit.py, serum-browser-test.py and
  campaign-browser-test.py all use the shared loader and each asserts that the
  bundle was delivered externally, not inline.
- New positive control `assert_inline_scripts_blocked()`: the harness injects a
  throwaway inline script under the served CSP and requires it to be rejected.
  It only claims proof when the response actually carried a CSP
  (`csp_from_headers`), so a static server without headers reports "not proven"
  instead of a false pass.
- New scripts/csp-axe-harness.test.mjs (offline, no browser): no harness may
  regress to inline injection, `_headers` must keep script-src 'self' without
  unsafe-inline/unsafe-eval, the test route must stay same-origin and absent
  from production files, and axe must not be copied into dist. Wired into
  `gates` and `gates:offline`.

Verification: npm run gates:offline -> 30 checks + 525 site checks, 260 unit
tests, 0 failures. The three browser harnesses still need their exact-head CI
run (Chromium + WebKit); the Playwright browser binaries cannot be downloaded
in this sandbox, so no claim is made that they were executed here.
